# MediaTek keeps most vendor libraries in a platform subdirectory
# (/vendor/lib64/mt6789/) and puts a symlink beside it at /vendor/lib64/,
# because the dynamic linker searches /vendor/lib64 and NOT the subdirectory.
# Stock ships 610 such links. Without them the libraries are installed but
# unreachable, and the failure looks like a missing library rather than a
# missing symlink.
#
# 427 are emitted here, generated 2026-09-19 from the stock vendor dump
# (ADVAN_6781_S34NF2_V4.0_20250304 weight: 409 point at mt6789/*, 11 are
# same-dir aliases in lib*/hw, 5 are bin/ platform links, 2 reconstructed
# below). Skipped, each for a stated reason:
#
#   180  vendor/bin/* -> toybox_vendor/toolbox. LineageOS already installs
#        working binaries at all of these paths, so emitting them produces
#        "overriding commands for target". Same exclusion class as the RS4
#        tree's six; Advan ships ~180 applets, not six.
#   3    absolute-target extraction artifacts (lib/modules, app/*/lib/*/*.so):
#        they point at /mnt/... paths that exist only on the extraction host.
#        The app/jni targets (vendor/lib64/lib{em_sensor,prizeem_sensor}_jni.so)
#        are noted for proprietary-files.txt Phase 2 -- the FILES are real,
#        only the links are broken.
#
# 2 rules are RECONSTRUCTED, not read: the extraction wrote them absolute
# (bin/v3avpud, bin/hw/...allocator...), and each is emitted relative with
# its target verified present in the dump. They are flagged on their lines.
#
# Overlap audit owed at Phase 2: every emitted (link, target) pair must be
# checked against all soong install rules (out/soong/installs-*.mk) and every
# PRODUCT_COPY_FILES destination, the way the RS4 tree checked its 640
# against 4596 + 758 paths. A prebuilt installing directly to a link path
# is an "overriding commands" parse error; a prebuilt installing to the
# TARGET path is fine (different paths).
#
# The link target MUST be baked into the recipe as a literal string (RS4
# lesson): a shared scratch variable is overwritten by definitions.mk
# macros before recipes run, and all links were once created pointing at a
# .pem file -- 635 dangling links, surfaceflinger never came up, no
# bootloop. $(2) below expands during $(call), so the recipe text contains
# the literal. Do not reintroduce a shared scratch variable here.
#
define 6781-symlink
$(eval $(TARGET_OUT_VENDOR)/$(strip $(1)): ; @mkdir -p $$(dir $$@); ln -sf $(strip $(2)) $$@) \
$(eval ALL_DEFAULT_INSTALLED_MODULES += $(TARGET_OUT_VENDOR)/$(strip $(1)))
endef

# Two app-partition JNI links. Stock ships them ABSOLUTE (/vendor/...), and
# they resolve on-device, so they are reproduced absolute -- unlike every
# rule below, which is relative. Targets verified present in
# proprietary-files.txt (both ship as blobs).
$(eval $(call 6781-symlink,app/SensorHub/lib/arm64/libem_sensor_jni.so,/vendor/lib64/libem_sensor_jni.so))
$(eval $(call 6781-symlink,app/HorCali/lib/arm64/libprizeem_sensor_jni.so,/vendor/lib64/libprizeem_sensor_jni.so))


$(eval $(call 6781-symlink,bin/dumpfaultd.mt6789,mt6789/dumpfaultd.mt6789))
